{% extends 'AdminInterfaceBundle:Layout:list.html.twig' %}
{% block listpane_content %}
	<section class="dp-paneblock dp-listpane">
		<header>
			<nav>
				{% include 'AdminInterfaceBundle:Layout:standard-settings-menu.html.twig' %}
			</nav>
			<h3>Agent Permission Groups</h3>
		</header>
		<article>
			<ul class="dp-item-list" dp-list-autoload>
				<li ng-repeat="group in ListCtrl.groups" dp-state-mark="agents.groups.edit.{{ ng_var('group.id') }}">
					<a href="{{ ng_href('agents.groups.edit', '{id: group.id}') }}">
						<div ng-if="group.sys_name" class="pull-right"><i class="fa fa-asterisk" style="position: relative; top: 3px;" tooltip="This is a built-in permission group." tooltip-placement="left"></i></div>
						<h4>
							<span class="title-id" title="ID">#{{ ng_var('group.id') }}</span>
							<span class="title-text">{{ ng_var('group.title') }}</span>
						</h4>
					</a>
				</li>
			</ul>
			<div class="dp-add-control">
				<a class="btn btn-default" href="{{ ng_href('agents.groups.create') }}">
					<i class="fa fa-plus"></i>
					{{ phrase('agent.general.add') }}
				</a>
			</div>
		</article>
	</section>
{% endblock %}
{% block listpane_help %}
	<header>
		<h1>Permission groups enable you to set permissions for groups of agents.</h1>
		<p>Agent <strong>permissions</strong> control what each agent is allowed to do. You can use these groups to quickly control permissions for many agents at once. The permissions for the group are applied to all agents who are members.</p>
	</header>
	<article>
		<section>


			<p>There are two built-in permission groups:</p>

			 <ul>
			 <li><strong>All Permissions</strong>  group enables agents who are members to do everything.</li>


			 <li><strong>All Non-Destructive Permissions</strong> lets agents do everything but delete content (and a few other potentially damaging actions, like writing mass replies to users).</li>
			</ul>

			<p>Click the permission groups to set which agents are members.</p>

			<p>You can add new groups and set which permissions they grant.</p>

			<p>Use the <strong>Departments</strong> tab to control access to tickets in each department:</p>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Full</strong> means the agent can view and work on tickets in that department</li>
				<li><strong>Assign</strong> means the agent can assign tickets to the department, but nothing more (they can't view them afterwards)</li>
			</ul>
			<p>You can separately set <strong>chat</strong> access for each department.</p>

			<p>When you add an agent to multiple permission groups, they get every permission that is granted by any of the groups.</p>


			<p>You can also grant an agent extra individual permissions beyond those they get from their permission groups from the <strong>Agents</strong> screen: these are called <strong>permission overrides</strong>.</p>
		</section>


		<section>
		<h2><span>FAQ</span></h2>
		<dl>
			<dt><em>Q:</em>I want to remove a permission from an agent, but why is it locked?</dt>
			<dd><em>A:</em>
				Groups and overrides always <em>add</em> permissions; you can't use an override to take away a permission granted by one of an agent's groups. To limit an agent's permissions, make sure that they are not a member of any groups which grant the permission you want to remove (including All Permissions and All Non-Destructive Permissions) .
			</dd>
		</dl>
</section>

			<section class="related-content">
			<h2><span>Related Content</span></h2>
			<ul>

				<li><i class="fa fa-book"></i> <a href="https://www.deskpro.com/manuals/admin-manual/admin-manual.html#agent-permissions" target="_blank">Agent permissions</a></li>
				<li><i class="fa fa-book"></i> <a href="https://www.deskpro.com/manuals/admin-manual/admin-manual.html#permission-overrides" target="_blank">Permission overrides</a></li>
				<li><i class="fa fa-book"></i> <a href="https://www.deskpro.com/manuals/admin-manual/admin-manual.html#agent-department-permissions" target="_blank">Agent department permissions</a></li>
				<li><i class="fa fa-file-text"></i> <a href="https://support.deskpro.com/kb/articles/256" target="_blank">Limiting agent access to tickets by department</a>
</li>
			</ul>
	</section>
	</article>
{% endblock %}
